  "section_notes": "S2 lets the regulator decide whether a model above 5% may keep selling, with no fixed end point, which is weaker than a mandatory sales stop and benefits Northwind's Hearth 10 (6.2%). S5 makes recall mandatory above 8 per 100,000 with no transition or corrective-action alternative, which directly affects Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9); S3's 24-month new-unit deadline sits outside the stated acceptable range, while the 6-year retrofit window benefits Northwind's low 38% shut-off share."
